From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP grass spread must not NPE into the cut

0065 kept west PLUGIN/FORCED chunks entity-ticking after the ticket wall.
Grass randomTick then getChunkAt a neighbor in the empty corridor (null)
and killed region #1 (ReportedException → whole server stop). Folia was
not designed for a live packed-spawn hole. Skip unloaded/cut neighbors;
do not sync-load the strip. Not bot herding. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/block/SpreadingSnowyBlock.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/block/SpreadingSnowyBlock.java
@@ -91,9 +91,13 @@
                         if (cachedChunk.locX == testPos.getX() >> 4 && cachedChunk.locZ == testPos.getZ() >> 4) {
                             access = cachedChunk;
                         } else {
-                            access = level.getChunkAt(testPos);
+                            // Packed-spawn cut: neighbor is the empty corridor. getChunkAt is null.
+                            access = level.getChunkIfLoaded(testPos);
                         }
+                        if (access == null) {
+                            continue;
+                        }
                         if (access.getBlockState(testPos).is(baseBlock.get()) && SpreadingSnowyBlock.canPropagate(access, defaultBlockState, testPos)) {
                             org.bukkit.craftbukkit.event.CraftEventFactory.handleBlockSpreadEvent(level, pos, testPos, defaultBlockState.setValue(SNOWY, isSnowySetting(access.getBlockState(testPos.above()))), Block.UPDATE_ALL); // CraftBukkit
                             // Paper end - Perf: optimize dirt and snow spreading
